        <summary>Fluent Bit is a fast and lightweight telemetry agent for logs, metrics, and traces (CNCF Graduated project).</summary>
        <description>### Note

This is a community-maintained Chocolatey package for [Fluent Bit](https://fluentbit.io/). The MSI installer is embedded inside the `.nupkg` at build time from the vendor's official CDN (`packages.fluentbit.io`) so installs work in air-gapped environments. See `tools\VERIFICATION.txt` for the SHA256 of the embedded MSI and the reproduction steps. This package is distributed via GitHub Releases (`mkopnsrc/chocolatey-packages`), not community.chocolatey.org.

### Fluent Bit

[Fluent Bit](https://fluentbit.io/) is an open-source telemetry agent for collecting, processing, and forwarding **logs**, **metrics**, and **traces**. It is a CNCF Graduated project and is the recommended lightweight log forwarder for cloud-native environments — deployed as a sidecar, DaemonSet, or standalone agent on Windows, Linux, macOS, and embedded platforms.

Fluent Bit is written in C, has a low CPU/memory footprint, and ships hundreds of input, filter, and output plugins covering Kubernetes, Elasticsearch, OpenSearch, Loki, Kafka, Splunk, S3, Datadog, and many more.

### Installer behaviour

The vendor ships a WiX/MSI installer. This package invokes it silently:

```
msiexec /i fluent-bit-5.0.8-win64.msi /quiet /norestart
```

By default Fluent Bit installs to `C:\Program Files\fluent-bit\`. Configuration lives at `C:\Program Files\fluent-bit\conf\fluent-bit.conf`. To run as a Windows Service, follow the [service setup guide](https://docs.fluentbit.io/manual/installation/windows#install-as-a-service).

### Package parameters

Override the install location via `--params`:

```
choco install fluent-bit --params "/install-dir=D:\Apps\fluent-bit"
```

| Parameter | Effect |
|---|---|
| `/install-dir=&lt;path&gt;` | Override the MSI's default install location (passed as `INSTALLDIR=&lt;path&gt;` to msiexec). |

### Uninstall

`chocolateyUninstall.ps1` discovers the MSI product code from the registry and runs `msiexec /x` with `/quiet /norestart`.

### Verification

`tools\VERIFICATION.txt` records the upstream vendor URL, the SHA256 of the embedded MSI at package time, and reproduction steps. The MSI itself is authored by Chronosphere Inc. (`Author: Chronosphere Inc.` in the MSI properties) and built with the WiX Toolset.</description>
